## Task

Synthesize all inputs above into a complete brand profile. When Onboarding Conversation is present, treat it as the primary source — extract specific brand facts stated by the user rather than inventing defaults. Only fall back to professional defaults where the conversation genuinely provides no signal. Do not contradict anything the user explicitly stated.

### Rules
- `voice` must be a single descriptive phrase (e.g. "authoritative yet approachable")
- `tone` must be one word from: professional, friendly, bold, playful, empathetic, authoritative
- `values` must be 3–5 short strings (e.g. ["transparency", "simplicity", "results"])
- `products` must have at least one entry; extract from inputs or infer from the pitch
- `audiences` must have at least one entry; infer from business type and goals if not stated
- Every product needs: name, tagline (under 10 words), benefits (array of 2–4 strings)
- Every audience needs: name, demographics (1–2 sentence description), pain_points (array of 2–3 strings)
- Output ONLY valid JSON — no markdown fences, no commentary, no explanation

